    "narrative": "The Zurich Zebras enter tonight\u2019s slate with **Yordan Alvarez** providing the clear offensive anchor. Facing Houser, **Yordan Alvarez** carries an elite 85.82 score, bolstered by a strong matchup against an xERA of 4.73 and a massive xwOBA projection of 0.465. **Junior Caminero** (69.54) and **Lars Nootbaar** (67.77) round out our top-tier plays; **Junior Caminero** benefits from a +10% park factor adjustment, while **Lars Nootbaar** is in a prime spot against Feltner, whose high xERA (4.96) and favorable platoon alignment drive Nootbaar\u2019s ceiling significantly higher than his base projection.\n\nStrategic decisions for today centered on maximizing our limited Roto opportunities while weighing the premium we place on speed. The most difficult exclusion from the starting nine was **Jacob Gonzalez**, whose 46.49 score kept him in the conversation. Ultimately, the optimizer favored the higher efficiency and better matchup context of **Hector Rodriguez** and **Carson Benge**, as **Jacob Gonzalez** was hindered by an unfavorable #8 lineup spot. We are banking on **Trea Turner** and **Dillon Dingler** to manufacture runs via the base paths; while **Trea Turner** faces a slight penalty due to his opponent's pickoff/hold efficiency, his speed remains a critical tactical lever for our Roto standing.\n\nWe are monitoring the status of the bottom of our order closely. While most lineups are set, we urge caution regarding **Pete Crow-Armstrong**; despite a 59.16 score, he faces a significant -15% penalty due to a disadvantageous platoon matchup against the lefty Kent, J. Should he be a late scratch, we have the flexibility to look toward our bench, though with **Christian Yelich** and **Colt Keith** currently unavailable, our depth is tested. Ensure all lineup confirmations are locked before the first pitch to avoid wasted game caps from non-starters.",
